Q2 — Reflect on your career interests
Have my interests evolved?
Yes. Leading the CAQ/CA process improvement and the ADR and cloud onboarding work this half has got me more interested in the governance side of EA — how the practice runs as a whole, not just individual solutions.
I've also become interested in the regulatory side of cloud — things like OSFI B-10, and the risks around relying too heavily on one cloud provider and being able to exit or move if needed. I've enjoyed learning how architecture supports staying compliant in a regulated financial company.
Taking on the Database Services Roadmap, which is outside my usual area, showed me I enjoy longer-term planning and working across different business units more than I expected.
Being the person other teams come to for advice on ARM and new projects has confirmed that the advisory, people-facing part of the job is where I do my best work.
What would help me keep growing?
Getting more involved in the big programs from start to finish.
More exposure to integration and modern technology work, so my impact reaches beyond just Cloud and DevOps.
Growing into a more senior architecture role over time, ideally one that includes leading people.
